    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get what u mean about the oxalate thing but i read online that vitamin c is a huge antioxidant and helps with inflammation so it might actually help the kidneys stay healthy in the long run? i feel like my doctor just gives me the same old \"drink more water\" advice which is super unhelpful. if i stay hydrated and take the 2000mg, isn't the water going to just flush it all out anyway? it seems like a pretty safe way to boost my health.",
