      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While vitamin C does have antioxidant and anti-inflammatory properties, the relationship between these benefits and kidney health is still being researched. Moreover, it's unlikely that 2000mg of vitamin C will be effectively flushed out of the body through drinking water alone, as water is not sufficient to excrete high amounts of this nutrient. Drinking 8-10 glasses of water may have a minimal effect, so high doses of vitamin C may still linger in the system. It's also worth noting that your doctor may have concerns about your overall kidney function and potential interactions with medications or other supplements, which you haven't mentioned.",
      "source": "target",
